      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;â€œCatra, you have to let me go.â€ Adora wasnâ€™t pleading but demanding. This did not sit well with Catra. Her smirk faltered for a split second before coming back twice as strong. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œThereâ€™s always something with you, isnâ€™t there Adora.â€ Catra crouched before her prisoner, cupping her cheek with a clawed hand. â€œSee the thing is, I donâ€™t have to do anything anyone tells me to anymore.â€ Adoraâ€™s eyes widened a little but kept her eyes trained on Catra who took this as an encouragement to continue. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œIâ€™m in control out here. This is my land now. And you,â€ Catraâ€™s gentle hand turned harsh, grabbing Adoraâ€™s chin earning a slight gasp. â€œWell, you are just an inconvenience.â€ &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;OR&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra decides to ditch the Horde and take the place as Ruler of the Crimson Waste&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
